No, L117 does not set a specific time period after which you are required to provide refresher training [L117, p. 17]. 

While you may decide that automatic refresher training or a retest after a set period (such as 3–5 years) is the best way to ensure competence, you must still monitor operator performance to determine if extra training is needed before that set period ends [L117, p. 17].

L117 states that refresher training or retesting may be appropriate in the following circumstances:
*   Operators have not used trucks for some time [L117, p. 17];
*   Operators are occasional users [L117, p. 17];
*   Operators appear to have developed unsafe working practices [L117, p. 17];
*   Operators have had an accident or near miss [L117, p. 17]; or
*   Operators have changed their working practices or environment [L117, p. 17].
